-- title:
--   Round-eight certificates of the integer-multiplication κ-record (κ = 12612978530233/10¹⁷)
-- statement:
--   The six computational certificates of round eight of the integer-multiplication κ-record (Jain, repository `integer-mult-kappa`, file `lean/Round8.lean`), checked exactly as published:
--
--   1. **Bit-phase rank sum.** For the bit-interchange histogram (one-run histogram, width classes up to $22$ plus a $484$-class and a $506$–$528$ tail range), the weighted rank sum $\sum w\,n$ equals $55\,395\,128\,481$.
--
--   2. **Bit-phase moment bound.** With savings $a = 25\,367/2\cdot 10^8$, base width $m = 529$ and work budget $W = 104\,719\,230$: every width $w < m$ and $a L_w < 1$ with $L_w = \operatorname{lnUp}(m/w)$, and $\sum n w/(m(1-a L_w)) < W$.
--
--   3. **Stopped saving.** With $a_{\text{old}} = 12\,899/2\cdot 10^8$ and $\theta = 1/1000$: $a_b = (1-\theta)a + \theta a_{\text{old}} = 6\,338\,633/5\cdot 10^{10}$ exactly, and $a_b < \theta$.
--
--   4. **Complex-phase rank sum.** For the complex-interchange histogram (completed-core sharing), $\sum w\,n = 7\,410\,813\,248$.
--
--   5. **Complex-phase exp-moment bound.** With $a = 3\,945\,999/31\,250\,000\,000$, $m = 576$, $W = 12\,869\,228$: every $w < m$, $a L_w < 4$, and $\sum n w e^{a L_w}/m < W$.
--
--   6. **Parameter assembly.** With the two savings above, $\beta = 1/1000$, $\varepsilon = 399\,949\,548\,085\,879/4\cdot 10^{14}$, $x = c_1 = 13\,093$, $m_c = 576$, $s_c = 7\,410\,813\,248$: the guard `kappaOK` holds and every cost margin exceeds $\kappa = 12\,612\,978\,530\,233/10^{17} \approx 1.26\cdot 10^{-4}$.
--
--   Round eight is the strongest published κ-record for integer multiplication; the κ-value here is the one targeted by `IntMul.Kappa.jain_round8`. Every claim is a finite computation over explicit rational data, discharged by `decide` in the Lean kernel.
-- source:
--   Swapnil Jain, integer-mult-kappa, https://github.com/Swapnil-jain/integer-mult-kappa, file lean/Round8.lean — the six round-eight certificates (generated by lean/gen.py from round8-histograms.json).

